---
import Shell from "../layouts/Shell.astro";
import Section from "@bundu/ui/Section.astro";

const ld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  url: "https://circles.mukoko.com/about",
  name: "About Mukoko Circles",
  isPartOf: { "@id": "https://circles.mukoko.com/#website" },
}).replace(/</g, "\\u003c");
---

<Shell
  title="About Mukoko Circles"
  description="What Circles are, how they work in the Mukoko super-app, and what this site shows and never shows."
  canonical="https://circles.mukoko.com/about"
  headExtra={`<script type="application/ld+json">${ld}</script>`}
>
  <section class="gradient-showcase border-b border-border">
    <div class="container-narrow py-16 md:py-20">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-h1 text-balance">What are Mukoko Circles?</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-muted-foreground">
        Circles are the communities of mukoko, Africa's privacy-first social
        super-app. A running club in Harare, a book club in Nairobi, a network
        of Lagos designers: each is a circle, with its own members, posts,
        events and chat.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section>
    <div class="container-prose space-y-10 px-0">
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">Circles live in the Mukoko app</h2>
        <p>
          There is no separate Circles app. You create, join and take part in
          circles inside the Mukoko super-app, alongside your events, messages
          and news. For now, circles sit inside Mukoko Events, where they lead
          with their gatherings and calendars.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site, circles.mukoko.com, is the front door: it lists the circles
          anyone can join, and gives every one of them a page you can share.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">Four kinds of circle</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Public:</strong> anyone can join and take part. Listed here.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Broadcast:</strong> the hosts post, and everyone can follow
            along. Listed here.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Private:</strong> people ask to join and the hosts approve.
            Never listed here.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Secret:</strong> invitation only, and invisible to everyone
            else. Never listed here.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">What this site shows, and what it never does</h2>
        <p>
          A circle's page shows its name, description, size and categories, and
          the posts its moderators have approved for the public. It never shows
          who the members are, and posts are shown as the circle's, not as any
          one person's.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything here comes from Mukoko's public directory. This site keeps
          no database of its own and sets no tracking cookies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-h3">Ubuntu, in practice</h2>
        <p>
          <em>Umuntu ngumuntu ngabantu</em>: a person is a person through other
          people. Circles exist so your people can find you, and so your
          community belongs to you, not to an algorithm.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/create">Create a circle</a>
        <a class="btn-outline" href="/circles">Browse circles</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Shell>
